INT. PAWNSHOP, BACK ROOM - NIGHT

Shelves of guitars, cameras, wedding rings under glass. A single dusty lamp. Tension thick as the smell.

SILAS "SILK" MERCADO, forties, in a silk shirt, leans on a safe. Four men face him in a loose arc: TWO-TON TOMMY, enormous; PEARL, thin and quick; BIG ARTHUR, grey-bearded; and young SWEETS, jittery, with a revolver tucked in his waistband.

SILK
Gentlemen.

TWO-TON TOMMY
Silk.

PEARL
You're late.

SILK
I'm exactly on time.

SWEETS
He's lying.

BIG ARTHUR
Quiet, boy.

Silk reaches for the safe dial. Sweets' hand twitches toward his waistband. Pearl and Tommy move together to block him, and Arthur steps between, and for a moment all four stand shoulder to shoulder, nobody breathing. The lamp flickers.

SILK
Easy. It's just the combination.

He spins the dial. A click. The door swings open on rows of bundled cash. Nobody moves.

PEARL
Count it.

SILK
Already did.
